{
 "test": 7520,
 "source": "NHTSA Vehicle Crash Test Database (public domain, US government)",
 "scenario": "S11",
 "summary": "2012 Toyota Camry LE 4-door (VIN 4T4BF1FK1CR157833), NCAP full-frontal into a rigid wall at 56.3 km/h, MGA Research, 2011-11-15. Test mass 1662.1 kg (curb 1459). 14 high-speed films at 1000 fps with each camera frame written 3 times; caption 0.00 ms at file frames 150-152 (all 14 films). Same sequence and timing as 8545 by eye in camera 3: hood tent by 30 ms, folded by 85 ms. Sensor: wall-force peaks 304 kN at 13 ms, 829 kN at 30 ms, 583 kN at 56 ms; maximum travel 0.685 m at 76 ms; rebound 0.89 m/s; separation 88.3 ms (report). Post-test (report): crush C1..C6 364, 478, 531, 535, 489, 400 mm (damage width 1282 mm); wheelbase -56 mm left, -52 mm right. Comparison with Rubble: engine/docs/crash-reference/camry-frontal-comparison.md.",
 "sources": [
  "report v07520R001.pdf (MGA NCAP-MGA-2012-027, 164 pages): PDF p. 10 (Data Sheet 1 cont., p. 6): weights (UVW 1459.0 kg, ATW 1662.1 kg, front/rear 946.8/715.3 kg), CG 1194 mm aft of front axle as tested, wheelbase 2774 mm",
  "PDF p. 18 (Data Sheet 6 cont., p. 14): camera table: cameras 2-15 at 1000 fps, cameras 1 and 18 real time 30 fps; 16 and 17 not used",
  "PDF p. 26 (Data Sheet 13, p. 22): impact 56.3 km/h, velocity change 59.7 km/h, time of separation 88.3 ms, crush profile C1-C6, damage width 1282 mm",
  "PDF p. 27 (Data Sheet 14, p. 23): wheelbase 2774 -> 2718 left, 2722 right; door openings unchanged",
  "PDF p. 3 (abstract), p. 5 and p. 25: maximum crush 579 mm at the centreline (length at centreline 4809 -> 4230 mm)",
  "report v07520R002.pdf: the airbag module's event data (Bosch CDR), not used here",
  "sensor curves: engine/docs/crash-reference/nhtsa/7520.json"
 ],
